<h2>How the calculation works</h2><p>Platform fees = order value × commission rate + fixed per-order fee. Contribution per order = order value − platform fees − food cost − packaging cost. Contribution margin divides that contribution by order value.</p><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Use this to test delivery-only menu pricing, channel mix or promotional discounts. A strong menu gross margin can shrink materially after aggregator commissions and packaging costs.</p><h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2><p>Real settlements may include GST on commissions, payment charges, ads, discounts funded by the restaurant, delivery subsidies, refunds and other adjustments. Add relevant per-order costs where possible or reconcile against actual settlement statements.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>Modeling several order values can show whether minimum-order thresholds or bundles improve contribution by spreading fixed fees and packaging cost.</p>
